  "published": "2026-11-13T14:06:31.457Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Rebuild every assembly that uses Idioma with this version. What generated code calls has moved to the namespace CodeChops.Idioma.Internals, so an assembly built with 0.1.0 does not run on 0.2.0.\n\nNew:\n- Your IDE offers a fix for LOC002 and LOC007.\n- Translated is on LocalizableText alone: ResourceText.Translated no longer compiles.\n- #pragma warning disable and [SuppressMessage] also silence what the generator reports.\n\nFixed:\n- An Android app registers its languages.\n- Generated code compiles for a text named like its namespace, and in a namespace that starts with Idioma, Generated, or Internals.\n- A text read from JSON that comes in as a stream skips a member it does not know.\n- A set named after a two-letter code is not taken for a longer code its name happens to end in.\n- A default-language set without a parameterless constructor gets LOC002, not a compiler error in generated code.\n- LOC016 also checks wording written as the initializer of a property.\n\nNo longer public: WithTranslation, LocalizableText.FromGeneratedCode, ResourceText.Create, and RegisterLanguages and RegisterLanguageCode of TranslationsRegistry.",
